extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.153-156. `mdc_base` CARRIES THE CONVERSION AS PROSE rather than using `mdc_from_hp_sdc`, and the difference is real: that flag turns hit points and the WHOLE S.D.C. total into M.D.C., where this class converts hit points and HALF the S.D.C. Using the flag would have quietly granted more M.D.C. than the book gives. An entire ability block is CONDITIONAL and therefore prose: in animal form the character gains +2 initiative, +1 strike, +2 dodge, +2 roll, +2 vs poison and disease and +10% to track by smell, none of which applies in her own shape - `bonuses` is unconditional by rule. The Horror Factor she can PROJECT by making herself look demonic (10, +1 per two levels) is likewise not a save she makes. THE LEVEL-UP PSIONIC GRANT IS AN EITHER/OR - one Super Psionic power or two lesser ones - which no schedule entry expresses across two counts; the schedule carries the Super Psionic half, exactly as it does on The Gifted One. The psionic category is `Super`, not the book''s ''Super Psionic'': that is the name regression refused The Gifted One for, and it is worth getting right the first time here. Two skill rows come from one slashed line again, Imitate Voices & Sounds and Impersonation."
